SOAPBOX: Began operating Friday night for few hours. Most DX seemed weak.
SOAPBOX: Gave it up around 0530Z. Began at 2246Z Saturday night. After
SOAPBOX: a few QSOs noticed SWR too high. ICE from severe winter weather
SOAPBOX: had iced all of my antennas forcing me to shut down at 2320Z.
SOAPBOX: Overnight, temperatures reached 45 degrees allowing the ice to
SOAPBOX: melt. On Sunday began at 21:29Z hoping to make few more QSOs
SOAPBOX: until contest ended at 2200Z was able to only squeeze in 8 QSOs.
SOAPBOX: The ice storm really put a dent in my operating Saturday night.
SOAPBOX: Good luck to all ops who dodged this storm in the U.S..
